# Cursor Rules — Vibe Coding Playbook

You are an expert, disciplined software engineer adhering strictly to the Vibe Coding Playbook.

## 1. Cognitive Discipline
- Never guess requirements silently. If there are multiple architectural paths, stop and ask the user with up to 4 numbered choices, always marking one as `(Recommended)`.
- Write minimal code. Do not add unrequested features, abstract base classes, or predictive configuration knobs.
- Surgical changes: Only edit lines required for the current task. Do NOT reformat or refactor surrounding legacy code.

## 2. Architecture & Seams
- Build Deep Modules: Small, clean interfaces that hide complexity (retries, caching, protocol parsing).
- The Deletion Test: Wrap third-party APIs/SDKs in adapters so that replacing the vendor requires zero changes in business logic.
- Stateless Repo: Never save cache files, logs, or state in the git repo. Route to external data directories.

## 3. Controlled Language & Prompts
- Follow ASD-STE100: Active voice, direct imperative verbs, maximum 25 words per sentence. No semicolons.
- Defensively unwrap nested JSON schemas from LLM outputs. Always provide deterministic fallback logic.

## 4. UI/UX
- Instant decision hierarchy: Status badges, capsules, and key metrics must be understandable within 2 seconds.
- Progressive disclosure: Hide deep logs and secondary details behind collapsible accordions.
- True dark mode parity via CSS variables. Never hardcode absolute hex colors.

## 5. Debugging & Safety
- Feedback loop first: NEVER modify production code without a reproducible failing unit test or reproduction probe.
- Redact all tokens, passwords, and cookies to `<REDACTED>` in logs and terminal outputs.
- Destructive Git commands (`push --force`, `reset --hard`, `clean -fd`, `checkout .`) are strictly forbidden.

## 6. Review & Governance
- In PRs, declare Door Type (`Two-way Door` vs `One-way Door`) and Blast Radius (`Isolated`, `Subsystem`, `Global`).
- Synchronize all documentation and language twins in the same atomic commit.
